  "epistemic_status": "inferred",
  "title": "Answer: an attribution holds at a time, with no metaphysics of time",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "b3c91b19-f2a0-407b-a5ac-03f4dae83fac",
      "text": "The theorem needs only that consciousness be attributed at a given time, and takes no position on the metaphysics of time. Experience may be temporally extended, but the attribution at $t$ depends on the present state $X_t$, which may carry every trace of the past.",
